WEBVTT

00:26:29.072 --> 00:26:32.438
I was that person for a long time.

00:26:32.462 --> 00:26:34.384
I had years and years of rejections.

00:26:34.408 --> 00:26:36.421
I've got files full of rejection letters,

00:26:36.445 --> 00:26:40.153
and I didn't like it.

00:26:40.177 --> 00:26:42.857
I didn't like people not liking my work.

00:26:42.881 --> 00:26:45.567
I didn't like getting letters back
from "The New Yorker"

00:26:45.591 --> 00:26:49.274
saying, "No, thank you" again and again
and again and again and again.

00:26:50.147 --> 00:26:53.118
But that wasn't what I was in it for.
That was a side effect.

00:26:53.142 --> 00:26:56.176
It's not that I didn't want to have
recognition and success,

00:26:56.200 --> 00:26:58.416
because I certainly did
and I certainly do.

00:26:58.440 --> 00:27:01.885
But the feeling that I would get
when I would get those letters